  "body": "It seems the current HTML specification doesn't define the initial value of [selectionDirection](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#selection-direction).\r\n\r\nThe initial state of INPUT and TEXTAREA is \"[a text entry cursor at the beginning of the control](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#concept-textarea/input-cursor).\"  ```selectionStart``` and ```selectionEnd``` in a case of text entry cursor are defined, but ```selectionDirection``` is not defined in such case.\r\n\r\nActual initial value in major UAs is \"none\" if the platform supports it, or \"forward\".  I remember some of WPT tests already imply it.\r\n\r\n",
